<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ha Giang province</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hà Giang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ha Giang was a mountainous province in the far north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, with a population largely of ethnic minorities such as the Hmong and Tày. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vi-xuyen">Vi Xuyen district</a> saw heavy border fighting with China between 1984 and 1989. In 2025 it was merged into Tuyên Quang province as part of a national reform of provinces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ha-giang-province.jpg" alt="Ha Giang province" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: haithanh · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C4%90%C3%A8o_M%C3%A3_P%C3%AC_L%C3%A8ng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
